      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes **how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure**. Specifically:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records the file\u0027s prior state\u2014either its previous content (if it existed) or notes that it didn\u0027t exist\u2014into an in-memory write journal.\n\n- If the agent run fails (due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or all attempted writes being denied), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n\n- This gives each run all-or-nothing semantics for its writes without needing a database transaction\u2014the journal itself serves as the transaction log, held in memory for the duration of one run.\n\nThe page also notes that the Query agent never uses this rollback path since it has no write tool at all.",
      "input_tokens": 2565,
      "output_tokens": 200
